    {
     "id": "notes-2",
     "blocks": [
      {
       "t": "prose",
       "md": "- **Range of $\\beta_\\pi$.** From 1. At $\\beta_\\pi = 1$ the real rate does not respond to inflation, $\\theta = 1$, and a supply shock passes one-for-one into inflation with output unchanged (the IS-MP curve is vertical at $y^*$). The case $\\beta_\\pi < 1$ is discussed in the concept note.\n- **Tests.** The notes' worked example ($\\theta = 2/3$; $\\pi_2 = 4$, $i_2 = 7$, $y_2 = 99$) and computed cases, each checked in Python against the three original equations."
      }
